__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Distribution / packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
*.egg

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Testing / coverage
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Finite-model verification output.
#
# The CI workflow writes these into the repo (`--out verification-artifacts`),
# and ci_gate.py refuses to pin a verification to a commit when the tree is
# dirty. Untracked-and-unignored, the artifacts the gate had just written made
# the tree dirty, so the gate failed itself: the run is PASS 19/19 when the
# same artifacts are written outside the tree. Ignoring the directory is what
# lets the workflow's own output stop invalidating its own provenance check.
verification-artifacts/
